From: Win7 port restore
Subject: [PATCH] desktop: point GUI brand references at the fork and add upstream attribution rows

The Win7 edition ships as GeniusTDY/cc-haha-win7, a fork of
NanmiCoder/cc-haha. Upstream v0.5.4 still carried the upstream
repo/author identity in every user-visible surface, so the port
repointed them at the fork while keeping proper attribution:

  * About page repo entry, sidebar GitHub icon, activity-settings
    default handle, all 5 locale defaultHandle values, package.json
    homepage/publish owner+repo, tauri.conf.json updater latest.json
    URL, backend DEFAULT_PROFILE_SUBTITLE and the matching test
    fixtures now reference GeniusTDY/cc-haha-win7.
  * Fork etiquette, two-row entries (identical card style, upstream
    row first):
      - About > repository: NanmiCoder/cc-haha (upstream) above
        GeniusTDY/cc-haha-win7 (this fork)
      - About > author: upstream author above the Win7 port
        maintainer
      - Activity settings default handle renders two links when the
        subtitle is still the default (custom subtitles keep the
        single-row rendering)
  * New i18n keys settings.about.upstreamHint / upstreamAuthorHint /
    forkMaintainerHint in zh, en, zh-TW, jp, kr (key sets stay
    aligned).

Action surfaces stay fork-only on purpose: the feedback button
(fork/issues), the changelog button (fork/releases) and the sidebar
icon point at the build users actually run; attribution lives on the
About page.

